  "notes": "EF-08 / m-25029102: the effects library v3. The SAME entries as v2, at the same versions, labels, stages, assets, params and max_per_part; only the smoke, ember and steam layers change: their loops are recorded (US$0, procedural: packages/creative/scripts/make_effect_loops.py, VP9 WebM on pure black, laid with a screen blend) and packaged at effects_assets/<id>/v1/preview.webm, so they are offered with their preview (preview_asset effects/<id>/v1/preview.webm, the same file the compose lays: video/layer_overlay.py). Their entry version stays 1, an EXPLICIT EXCEPTION to the rule below: v3 only offers them, fills their empty preview_asset and adds categories, while their params and asset folder effects/<id>/v1/ did not change; nobody could use version 1 while it was not offered, and the editor sends version 1. A future change of a loop (other bytes in v1/) does require a v2/ folder and an entry at version 2. v1 and v2 keep reading exactly as they were (the layers unoffered there). An effect is never edited in place: a change of parameters, prompt or asset is a new entry at version + 1. Categories (Deivid, 2026-11-16): every entry names at least one category from a closed set of stable Spanish ids (comida, texto, transicion, movimiento, general) so the screen can FILTER; a category never hides an effect and offered alone says what the screen offers, the same for every business. v1 and v2 have no categories.",
